  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.6.0 — configurable global search (basin-hopping) with a scale-aware default. fit_ecm gains a global_search_options object (temperature_mode 'relative'|'greedy'|'absolute', relative_temperature, absolute_temperature, step_size_decades), applied when fit_mode='global'. The Metropolis acceptance default changes from a raw absolute temperature (T=1.0, whose aggressiveness depended on the objective's scale) to a scale-aware relative temperature (0.1) — the same default now used by the engine, the app, and MCP. Absolute temperature is retained as an advanced/compatibility option; greedy rejects every worse basin. Step size is expressed in base-10 decades (step_size_decades; 0.5 ≈ up to 3.16x per hop). 39 tools (unchanged).",
